<title>USA: Triarc sees beverage, restaurant sales of $1 bln.</title>
<headline>Triarc sees beverage, restaurant sales of $1 bln.</headline>
<dateline>CEDAR RAPIDS, Iowa 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Triarc Cos Inc said Thursday it expected 1997 sales of nearly $1 billion through its Snapple, Mistic and Royal Crown beverage brands and its Arby's restaurants.</p>
<p>The outlook was part of a statement issued by the company summarizing earnings for its National Propane Partners Lp subsidiary for the second fiscal quarter ended June 30, 1997.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787))</p>
</text>
